This is a heuristic answer, not a verified derivation. I did not carry out the homological computations for B_r, so treat it as a best guess.

The reasoning behind the guess: T is a Nakayama-type algebra on N vertices with Loewy length ℓ = 4r+4 and N = (r+1)ℓ. The construction of B_r as a one-point-extension-style triangular matrix algebra with the dual-extension-like module U of length h = 2r+2 suggests that the finitistic dimension of B_r^op is attained at a module of projective dimension 2r+1, and that ddell (the derived-dimension-type invariant) matches this value. The two entries are set equal to 2r+1 on that basis.

